# docs/MINER.md
# Miner Guide

## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

Contributions to SN118 are MIT-licensed under the Ditto Contributor License Agreement (CLA). Before uploading miner agents or claiming bounty rewards, miners must sign the active CLA version using their hotkey.

### 1. Check CLA Status

Check whether your miner hotkey has signed the current CLA version:

```bash
uv run ditto cla status --wallet-name <wallet> --hotkey-name <hotkey>
```

### 2. Sign the CLA

To review and execute the CLA:

```bash
uv run ditto cla sign --wallet-name <wallet> --hotkey-name <hotkey>
```

The CLI will:
1. Fetch the effective CLA text from Platform and verify its SHA-256 digest.
2. Prompt for explicit typed confirmation (`I AGREE`).
3. Sign the canonical message (`ditto-cla:v1:<netuid>:<cla_version>:<cla_sha256>:<hotkey>:<nonce>:<issued_at>`) with the hotkey's sr25519 keypair.
4. Record the signature on Platform.

### 3. Rollout & Enforcing

The Platform submission gate transitions across three modes:
- `off`: Gate checks are bypassed.
- `shadow`: Missing signatures are logged and monitored on Backroom dashboards, but uploads proceed.
- `enforce`: Uploads from hotkeys without an active signature are rejected.

When maintainers publish a new CLA version (e.g. `v2`), hotkeys must execute `uv run ditto cla sign` again before submitting.
